All agent skill mirrors (.codex/skills, .agents/skills) are now gitignored
and generated at `forge setup` from canonical skills/; none are committed.

- listCodexSkillEntries reads from skills/ (not .codex/skills); the global
  $CODEX_HOME/skills install is generated from canonical skills/ with the
  stage adapter injected.
- forge setup generates .codex/skills (new) alongside .agents/skills and
  .claude/.cursor mirrors via populateAgentSkills.
- .gitignore ignores .agents/skills + .codex/skills; git rm --cached untracks
  both (~90 files); .codex/config.toml stays tracked.
- package.json files: drop .codex/ (nothing else needed there; config.toml is
  a repo-local dev artifact generated by tooling, not shipped). skills/ and
  .claude/skills/ still ship.
- Docs/comments updated: committed-mirror -> generated-at-setup across
  skills-sync.js, codex-skills.js, harness-capability-matrix.js, .gitignore,
  AGENTS.md skill-sync learning, AGENT_SKILL_PARITY.md.

NOTE: change-list item 2 (codex.plugin.json directories.skills -> "skills")
was intentionally NOT applied — it breaks the release-readiness bd-audit
classifier (which derives skill-surface classification from directories.skills)
and is not needed for single-sourcing (listCodexSkillEntries hardcodes skills/).
directories.skills stays ".codex/skills", consistent with claude/cursor mirrors.

Tests: added codex-skills positive read-from-skills/ test + populateAgentSkills
generates-both-mirrors test; repointed shepherd/skills-sync/agents-discovery/
package-distribution assertions off committed mirrors to setup-generated /
absence-tolerant checks.

